{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00426","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00426@rel:R25-11#cb5662c2","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00426","release":"R25-11","content":"function ResetKey [SWS_PER_00426] Upstream: RS_PER_00003 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; ResetKey ( ara::core::StringView key) noexcept; Resets a key of this Key-Value Storage to its initial value. ResetKey allows to reset a single key to its initial value. If the key is currently not available in the Key-Value Storage, it is re-created. Afterwards, the key-value pair will appear in both cases as if it was newly installed from the current Target Configuration. ResetKey will fail with kInitValueNotAvailable when neither Application Design nor Target Configuration define an initial value for the key. ResetKey may be delayed by an ongoing call from another thread to RemoveAllKeys, SyncTo Storage, or DiscardPendingChanges, or to SetValue, GetValue, GetCurrentValueSize, Remove Key, RecoverKey, or ResetKey for the same key-value pair. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/key_value_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::KeyValueStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kIllegalWrite rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td key td The key to be reset. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Access td Returned if the Key-Value Storage is configured as read- only. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be written because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption or decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kInitValueNotAvailable td rollback_semantics Returned if no intitial value was configured for this key. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the initial value. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the initial value would exceed the configured maximum AllowedSize of the Key-Value Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating or checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"e0a0bcd95636"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00426","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"ResetKey","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_KeyValueStorage_e55123.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-b045d30e3c97fa76","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":90,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ResetKey API in KeyValueStorage","n":16,"cap":"","sha":null,"nser":0,"src":"matrix"},{"id":"FIG-67a0c9934f8b513a","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":55,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"KeyValueStorage ResetKey method","n":14,"cap":"","sha":null,"nser":0,"src":"matrix"},{"id":"FIG-ac91624831463d